  median_empire: "The Median lancer rode the famed Nisaean horses of the Iranian plateau and was the direct forerunner of the Persian heavy cavalry that would dominate the East. Median horsemanship set the standard the Achaemenids inherited.",
  persia: "The Immortals were the ten-thousand-strong elite standing infantry of the Achaemenid kings, so named, the Greeks said, because every man who fell was instantly replaced to keep their number exactly constant. Splendidly equipped, they were the guard and shock force of the empire.",
  parthia: "The Parthian horse archer perfected the 'Parthian shot', twisting in the saddle to loose arrows backward at a gallop while feigning flight — the tactic that destroyed a Roman army at Carrhae. He was the elusive master of the open plain.",
  sassanid_persia: "The Savaran were the elite armoured cataphracts of Sassanid Persia, fully mailed riders on armoured horses who formed the iron core of the imperial army. Their thunderous charge anchored the long Persian wars against Rome.",
  egypt: "The maryannu chariot was the strike arm of New Kingdom Egypt, a light, fast two-horse vehicle bearing an archer who could rain arrows on the enemy and wheel away. It carried the pharaohs to their great victories in Syria and Nubia.",
  kush_nubia: "Nubia was called Ta-Seti, the 'Land of the Bow', and its archers were so feared that even Egypt eagerly recruited them. The Nubian archer was the deadly missile soldier of the Kushite kings.",
  carthage: "Carthage fielded the North African war elephant, made immortal by Hannibal's audacious crossing of the Alps to carry the war into Italy itself. Towering over the battlefield, it was Carthage's signature instrument of terror.",
