  mycenaean_greece: "Mycenaean spearmen, armoured in heavy bronze like the famous Dendra panoply, were the warrior-aristocrats of Homer's heroic age. They were the champions whose deeds echoed down into Greek epic.",
  greece: "The hoplite, the armoured citizen-soldier who fought behind a great round shield in the close ranks of the phalanx, defined Greek warfare and won the wars against Persia. Each was a free citizen fighting for his own city.",
