  han_china_cho_ko_nu: "Repeating Fire is the chu-ko-nu itself: the magazine-fed repeating crossbow attributed to Zhuge Liang, trading punch for a rate of fire nothing else in the ancient world matched.",
  china_tang_song_fire_lancer: "Fire Lance is the world's first gunpowder weapon, strapped to a pike: Song manuals show the huo qiang spitting flame ahead of a braced spear line — which is why the brace remains.",
  crete_cretan_archer: "Arrow Storm reflects antiquity's most-hired bowmen: Cretan mercenaries served Alexander, the Hellenistic kings and Rome precisely for the density of fire a Cretan company could lay down.",
  numidia_numidian_cavalry: "Fire & Retreat and Hide are Numidian warfare as Livy describes it: bridleless riders who attacked, scattered, and re-formed at will, impossible to pin and fatal to pursue.",
