  ayyubids_ayyubid_faris: "Feigned Retreat and Harry are Hattin, 1187: Saladin's riders lured the Crusader army into waterless hills, harried it past exhaustion, and destroyed it — the campaign this kit replays.",
  mamluks_mamluk: "Shock Charge and Fire & Retreat are the furusiyya curriculum itself: Cairo's academies drilled each mamluk to master both the couched lance and the bow at the gallop — Ain Jalut proved the pairing.",
  almoravids_lamtuna_spearman: "War Drums and Last Stand are Zallaqa, 1086: the Almoravid drums — the first Iberia had heard — panicked men and horses, while the veiled Lamtuna line behind them famously did not retreat.",
  swahili_swahili_dhow: "Monsoon Run and Boarding Party reflect Indian Ocean seamanship: dhow captains timed everything to the monsoon winds, and coastal fighting meant grappling a hull, not sinking it.",
  benin_ogboni_guard: "Sunder reflects the Oba's enforcers and the bronze-casting guilds behind them: the ada and ẹbẹn state swords of Benin were instruments of an authority that broke resistance.",
  kongo_kongo_archer: "Poisoned Arrows is documented Kongo practice: early Portuguese accounts describe central African archers whose envenomed shafts made even a graze a wound that kept killing.",
  // Mediterranean & Europe (second wave)
  rome_legionary: "Pilum Volley and Testudo are the legion's drill-book: every legionary carried two pila to hurl in the last strides before the gladius came out, and the tortoise of locked shields walked armies through arrow-storm sieges.",
  minoans_minoan_bireme: "Ram and Harry reflect the first thalassocracy: Thucydides credits Minos with clearing the Aegean of pirates — a navy built to run raiders down, pin them, and finish them.",
