  bulgaria_bulgar_horse_archer: "Mountain Ambush is the Vărbitsa Pass, 811: Krum walled the Byzantine army into a Balkan defile and destroyed it — Emperor Nikephoros' skull became the khan's drinking cup. Bulgar riders fought best from the high passes.",
  serbia_pronoia_knight: "Wedge Charge is the inheritance in the unit's own name: pronoia is the Byzantine land-grant system Serbia adopted wholesale, and Dušan's knights — crowned by an emperor styled 'of the Serbs and Greeks' — fought by the Byzantine book.",
  bohemia_hussite_war_wagon: "Wagenburg is Jan Žižka's invention entire: war wagons chained into an instant fortress, crossbows and handguns firing from behind the walls — five crusades broke against it and the blind general never lost a battle.",
